(Bug #45 — the declared-return control. Declaring the return type is the fix
 the diagnostic asks for, so every position the undeclared call is now refused
 in has to read a declared one back as what it is.)

To 'declared label'. Return a text, "hi".

print 'declared label'.
print "got {'declared label'}".

a list called items is [].
append 'declared label' to items.
print element 1 of items.

a list called literal is ['declared label', "second"].
print element 1 of literal.

a map called labels is {}.
set labels's "first" to 'declared label'.
print labels's "first".

a value called carried is 'declared label'.
print carried.
